  </section>

  <section id="faq" class="faq-section" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
    <header class="section-header section-header-plain">
      <h2 id="faq-title">Questions before you use NavishAI</h2>
      <p>Direct answers about customer communication, existing tools, and self-hosted operation.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <details class="faq-item" open>
        <summary>Who sends a customer message?</summary>
        <p>Only a signed-in teammate who reviews the current draft and deliberately presses Send. Automated work cannot schedule or trigger that message later.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Does NavishAI replace Intercom?</summary>
        <p>No. NavishAI can work beside Intercom and shared email, adding investigation, evidence, Account context, review, and an attributable final action.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>How does a cited draft handle weak evidence?</summary>
        <p>Material claims can be supported, stale, conflicting, uncertain, or refused. Missing or unreliable evidence stays visible during review instead of being presented as fact.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>What happens if memory or a model is unavailable?</summary>
        <p>NavishAI shows the degraded state and keeps core case work available. It does not silently switch customer data to a managed memory service.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Where do model credentials stay?</summary>
        <p>Subscription credentials stay on the customer-controlled execution host. NavishAI does not import, display, or store those login tokens.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Can we use our own health scorecard?</summary>
        <p>Yes. Teams can propose, preview, backtest, publish, version, and roll back a scorecard while keeping generated analysis separate.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Is there a hosted trial or a compliance certification?</summary>
        <p>No. This page does not offer a hosted trial or managed plan, and NavishAI does not claim SOC 2, HIPAA, ISO 27001, or any other certification.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-section" id="get-started" aria-labelledby="cta-title">
    <div class="cta-artwork">
      <%= image_tag "agent-cta-background.png", alt: "Saturated blue call-to-action background", class: "cta-image" %>
      <div class="cta-copy">
        <h2 id="cta-title">Already running<br>NavishAI?</h2>
        <div class="cta-action">
          <%= link_to "Sign in to your workspace", new_session_path, class: "button cta-button" %>
          <span>For an existing self-hosted deployment.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <footer class="landing-footer" id="footer">
    <div class="footer-top">
      <div class="footer-brand">
        <%= render "layouts/wordmark" %>
        <p>Evidence-backed Support and Customer Success work, with the final customer message kept in human hands.</p>
        <ul class="footer-marks">
          <li><span>Self-hosted</span></li>
          <li><span>Evidence-backed</span></li>
          <li><span>Human-controlled</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="footer-columns">
        <div>
          <h3>Product</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="#how-it-works" data-action="landing-header#jump">Support workflow</a></li>
            <li><a href="#features" data-action="landing-header#jump">Customer context</a></li>
            <li><a href="#self-host" data-action="landing-header#jump">Self-hosting</a></li>
            <li><a href="#faq" data-action="landing-header#jump">FAQ</a></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Operators</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><%= link_to "Sign in", new_session_path %></li>
            <li><%= link_to "Reset password", new_password_path %></li>
